!function(){"use strict";window.TDB_MISSION_OUTREACH_PACKS=[{id:"hospital",title:"Hospital & bedside visits",tagline:"Quiet verses when the room feels small",intro:"Use these to read aloud, leave on a tray, or pray through slowly. No hurry—let one verse settle before the next.",verses:[{ref:"Psalm 23:1-4",text:"The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want. He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters. He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name's sake. Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.",blurb:"Shepherd care in plain sight: God walks the valley, not only the meadow."},{ref:"Isaiah 41:10",text:"Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.",blurb:"A steady word for shallow breathing and noisy monitors—presence before explanation."},{ref:"Philippians 4:6-7",text:"Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God. And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.",blurb:"Trade the spiral for prayer and thanks—even tiny ones—and make room for peace."},{ref:"Psalm 46:1",text:"God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.",blurb:"Short enough to memorize at the door; strong enough to carry back to the chair."},{ref:"2 Corinthians 1:3-4",text:"Blessed be God, even the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of mercies, and the God of all comfort; Who comforteth us in all our tribulation, that we may be able to comfort them which are in any trouble, by the comfort wherewith we ourselves are comforted of God.",blurb:"Comfort is not a lecture—it is passed hand to hand under the same mercy."}],closing:"Lord, be nearer than the pain, quieter than the fear, and truer than the worst news. Give us words when we have none, and rest when we watch through the night. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{id:"grief",title:"Grief & funeral comfort",tagline:"Scripture for the ache that does not hurry",intro:"Read slowly. It is enough to let the Lord draw near—no fixing, no rushing the tears.",verses:[{ref:"Psalm 34:18",text:"The LORD is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.",blurb:"God does not stand back from grief—He draws near to the break."},{ref:"Matthew 5:4",text:"Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.",blurb:"Jesus blesses sorrow that is real—not hollow cheer, but promised comfort."},{ref:"Psalm 147:3",text:"He healeth the broken in heart, and bindeth up their wounds.",blurb:"Healing can be quiet work; He binds what is torn open."},{ref:"Psalm 30:5",text:"For his anger endureth but a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning.",blurb:"Not a deadline on grief—rather a sure dawn after the long night."},{ref:"Revelation 21:4",text:"And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.",blurb:"The last word on loss is not silence forever, but God wiping tears Himself."}],closing:"Father of mercies, meet us in this mourning. Carry what we cannot lift, and hold fast to every soul you love. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{id:"prison",title:"Prison & jail ministry",tagline:"Truth for locked doors and listening ears",intro:"These verses honor visitation, letter writing, and prayer for the incarcerated—Christ did not forget the cell.",verses:[{ref:"Hebrews 13:3",text:"Remember them that are in bonds, as bound with them; and them which suffer adversity, as being yourselves also in the body.",blurb:"Solidarity in Christ: remember as if you stood beside them."},{ref:"Psalm 142:7",text:"Bring my soul out of prison, that I may praise thy name: the righteous shall compass me about; for thou shalt deal bountifully with me.",blurb:"Honest prayer from depths—freedom that begins in the soul before the gate opens."},{ref:"Acts 16:25",text:"And at midnight Paul and Silas prayed, and sang praises unto God: and the prisoners heard them.",blurb:"Worship in the dark can be a witness when words fail."},{ref:"Isaiah 61:1",text:"The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon me; because the LORD hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound;",blurb:"Jesus' mission includes good news to the bound—liberty in His name."},{ref:"Psalm 119:11",text:"Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee.",blurb:"A verse carried inside can outlast what the walls keep out."}],closing:"Lord, you are not far from any cell. Strengthen visitors, chaplains, and those inside—let your Word find ground even where hope feels thin. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{id:"newbeliever",title:"New believer & evangelism",tagline:"Clear anchors for new life in Christ",intro:"Share gently—one verse at a time. Salvation is God's gift; growth is His patience in us.",verses:[{ref:"John 3:16",text:"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.",blurb:"Love moves first—belief receives what God already gave."},{ref:"Romans 10:9-10",text:"That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved. For with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation.",blurb:"Heart-truth and honest words—salvation is not a secret performance."},{ref:"Romans 10:13",text:"For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved.",blurb:"The door is wide—calling on Jesus is enough."},{ref:"Ephesians 2:8-9",text:"For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast.",blurb:"Grace means no earning—faith receives the gift."},{ref:"2 Corinthians 5:17",text:"Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.",blurb:"New birth is God's work—a real beginning, not a fresh coat of paint."}],closing:"Lord, open eyes to Jesus, seal new faith with your Spirit, and give boldness that stays humble. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{id:"missionary",title:"Missionary encouragement",tagline:"Strength for goers, senders, and intercessors",intro:"For those far from home, those who send, and those who pray—God finishes what He starts.",verses:[{ref:"Matthew 28:19-20",text:"Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost: Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world. Amen.",blurb:"The commission comes with a promise—His presence to the end."},{ref:"Isaiah 52:7",text:"How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace; that bringeth good tidings of good, that publisheth salvation; that saith unto Zion, Thy God reigneth!",blurb:"Peaceful feet on hard roads still look beautiful to heaven."},{ref:"Romans 10:14-15",text:"How then shall they call on him in whom they have not believed? and how shall they believe in him of whom they have not heard? and how shall they hear without a preacher? And how shall they preach, except they be sent? as it is written, How beautiful are the feet of them that preach the gospel of peace, and bring glad tidings of good things!",blurb:"Sending and going belong together—faith comes by hearing."},{ref:"Philippians 1:6",text:"Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ:",blurb:"Homesickness and harvest both yield to His finishing grace."},{ref:"Psalm 67:2",text:"That thy way may be known upon earth, thy saving health among all nations.",blurb:"Prayer for global glory—earth knowing His way, not our noise."}],closing:"Lord, keep your servants. Feed the weary, guard the lonely, and let the gospel sound clear. Bless senders and goers alike. In Jesus' name, Amen."}]}();